# ZAYA website — environment placeholders. NEVER commit real values.
# Real secrets live ONLY in Netlify → Site settings → Environment variables.

# Website AI Assistant (CR-027/ADR-024). Generate a free key at
# https://aistudio.google.com → "Get API key", then set it in Netlify env —
# see docs/ASSISTANT-SETUP.md. The assistant's curated answers work WITHOUT
# this key; only the English AI-fallback needs it.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the model (defaults to gemini-2.5-flash).
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# CMS OAuth relay (already configured in Netlify env; listed here for completeness).
GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── The assistant gate (founder ruling 2026-08-20) ──────────────────────────
# The AI assistant is OFF by default and has its OWN switch — it is NOT tied to
# site.json "published". See docs/ASSISTANT-GATE.md.
#
# The SHARED SECRET the relay requires. NO VALUE HERE, EVER — real values live
# only in Netlify → Site configuration → Environment variables (scope: Branch
# deploys). Must be >= 24 chars of A-Z a-z 0-9 _ - . With this unset:
#   * the build emits NO assistant markup at all (fail-closed), and
#   * /api/assistant answers 503 to everyone.
ZAYA_ASSISTANT_TOKEN=

# Optional switch: exactly "on" or "off" (anything else = off).
#   on  -> this build/context ships the widget (needs the token above too)
#   off -> kill switch; beats everything, including assistant.json enabled:true
# netlify.toml already sets "on" for the preview/assistant branch context and
# "off" for production. Leave blank locally unless you are testing the widget.
# ZAYA_ASSISTANT=
